# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Secrets
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
.env
.env.*
!.env.example

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Documentation
#
# docs/ is deliberately NOT ignored. CLAUDE.md section 2 names
# docs/architecture.md and docs/deployment-strategy.md as the project's source
# of truth, and a source of truth a fresh clone cannot read is not one.
# Do not add a docs/ pattern here — several Python and Node .gitignore
# templates ship one for Sphinx or generated API docs, and it would silently
# untrack the design documents.
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Python
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
__pycache__/
*.py[cod]
*$py.class
*.so
.Python
build/
dist/
sdist/
wheels/
*.egg-info/
*.egg
.eggs/
.venv/
venv/
ENV/
.pytest_cache/
.ruff_cache/
.mypy_cache/
.coverage
.coverage.*
coverage.xml
htmlcov/

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Django
#
# Migrations are NOT ignored — CLAUDE.md invariant 14 requires them in the repo.
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
*.log
staticfiles/
mediafiles/
celerybeat-schedule
celerybeat.pid

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Node / Next.js
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
node_modules/
.next/
out/
.turbo/
.eslintcache
*.tsbuildinfo
next-env.d.ts

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Editors and OS
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
.DS_Store
Thumbs.db
.idea/
*.swp
.vscode/*
!.vscode/extensions.json

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Claude Code's working directory
#
# Local and not shared. Three things live here and none of them belongs in the
# repository:
#
# - `settings.local.json` — per-developer, and named by the tool to say so.
# - `launch.json` — the dev-server entry an agent uses to open a preview. Useful,
#   but it describes one machine's setup rather than the project's.
# - `skills-temp/` — 2.3 MB and **a git clone of its own**, from
#   github.com/Mindrally/skills. An embedded repository is the one thing here
#   that would actively misbehave if staged: git records a gitlink rather than the
#   files, and the result is a directory that is empty for everyone who clones.
#
# Ignored as a whole rather than file by file, because the contents are whatever a
# session happened to need. If a launch entry is ever worth sharing, un-ignore
# that one path deliberately.
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
.claude/
